Vocaline's patch to CrispASR v0.8.42 (MIT, Copyright (c) the CrispASR authors; see its
LICENSE, installed beside this package's licence). Not part of upstream CrispASR.

Add --stream-short-context-sec N (default 0, off). In stream mode, an utterance shorter
than the 2 s redecode minimum is never decoded again: its final is the stitched partial
of its VAD slice alone, often too little audio for a multilingual model to settle on the
language (a short French phrase comes back in English). With N > 0, such an utterance is
decoded again with up to N s of the audio before it, starting no earlier than the
previous utterance and the rolling window, and only the tokens stamped after the middle
of the silence between the two, and none from more than 1 s before the utterance, are
kept. Without a previous utterance in the window, under 2 s combined, or without token
timestamps, the stitched fallback is used as before. With N = 0 the output is unchanged.

The range and the token cut are pure helpers in crispasr_stream_finalize.h, covered by
tests/test-stream-finalize.cpp.

